          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "the flower-heads of one or another of various plants considered to have anthelmintic properties (i.e. of use against intestinal worms), such as swine's fennel or sulphurwort (OED s.v. wormseed); in particular the dried unexpanded flower-heads of species of Artemisia, produced in Turkestan, used medically against intestinal worms; Levant or Alexandrian wormseed (OED s.v. santonica, Stieda, Venice, 107) (see also pulvis pro vermibus, semen lumbricorum)"
    }
  ],
